    "ceiling_height_rule": {
      "group": "interior",
      "binding": "specified",
      "status": "drafted",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "judgment": true,
      "rule": "Ceiling height is not derived by a harmonic mean of the room's own plan proportion. It follows the storey and the general scale of a two-storey courtyard block; the governing dimension is the viga (roof beam) span setting room depth, not a proportioned ceiling height.",
      "note": "OVERRIDES a cascade fill from renaissance-classical (a harmonic-mean-of-plan-proportion rule) reached via the churrigueresque/spanish-plateresque -> italian-renaissance lineage chain. This contradicts the node's own bound room-role pack: this style's own proportion_packs binds `room-vernacular` (precedence 1) as a judgment binding specifically because 'span-limited breadth and single-pile daylight depth are exactly what room-vernacular encodes' (the node's own note), and its own governing_logic states plainly that the proportional system is 'the arcade bay and the viga,' not a harmonic module. Confirmed with `resolve_kit.py mexican-colonial --slot ceiling_height_rule --verbose`, whose PACK RESOLUTION shows room-vernacular, not room-harmonic, as the pack that actually governs this slot by precedence. Fixed here per WP-4.2 instructions rather than on any ancestor kit; the identical fix is made on mexican-hacienda.kit.json for the same reason."
    },
