      "rule": "At religious sites, the church is set back from the street within its walled atrio, with a processional route around it, rather than built to the street line.",
      "note": "mexican-colonial.c05 (soft): 'Placing a colonial-type church on the street line removes the element that most distinguishes New Spain from Spain.' Held at judgment because the constraint is soft and cultural, not a hard geometric rule."
